====================================================================================================
G158 -- THE n-FOOTING DISCRIMINATOR: deep-end data vs n = 2.000 / 1.660
====================================================================================================

--- PART 0: THE MAPPING (derived, no data) ---
  one-function reading : g_obs = g_N mu(x), x = g_N/a0, mu(x) ~ x^(n-1) deep
  the deep RAR slope   : d log g_obs/d log g_N = 1 + d ln mu/d ln x -> n
  task-declared relation: the deep slope -> n/2, i.e. the deep end reads n = 2*beta
  seesaw (H046/G002)   : n = Lambda^2/(a0 M_Pl) = s_Lambda/a0, s_Lambda = 2 a0_DE
    n(a0_DE = 9.36190e-11) = 2.0000   (H046: 2.000147)
    n(a0_ALT = 1.12790e-10) = 1.6601   (H046: 1.660181)
    predicted deep slope beta = n/2 :  1.000 (DE footing)  vs  0.830 (ALT footing)
  program's own family mu_n(u) = 1-(1+u)^(-n), u = g/s: mu ~ n*u deep for
    EVERY n (linear in u): the deep RAR slope = 1/2 identically, n is the
    AMPLITUDE (the seesaw): a0 = s/n.  Two channels to n are therefore kept:
    slope channel n = 2*beta (the task mapping; measures the FORM = quadratic
    asymptote) and amplitude channel n = s_Lambda/a0_eff (a0_eff = g_obs^2/g_N,
    the seesaw itself).
  generic-law anchor: the committed quadratic RAR g_obs^2 = g_N^2 + a0 g_N has
    beta -> 1/2 exactly at x -> 0 and beta in [0.50, 0.58] over x in [0, 0.2]:
    its own window-exponent is n = 2*beta ~ 1.05-1.15, NOT 2.000 nor 1.660.

--- PART 1: THE SAMPLES (deep window g_N/a0_DE < 0.2) ---
  MIGHTEE-HI (G099): 80 rings / 18 galaxies; deep window g_N<0.2 a0_DE: 72 rings (90%)
  SPARC (G071): 641 rings / 35 galaxies; deep window: 409 rings / 35 galaxies
  HI dwarfs (G114, LT): 26 single points; deep g_bar<0.2 a0: 25/26 (the LITTLE THINGS sample IS the deep end);
    registered V_max-based deep tail g_N<0.1 a0: 7/26 (G114), median r log10(obs/pred) -0.094 -- context only; the RAR slope uses g_bar = G M_b/R^2.

