MIGHTEE         72     0.447  0.046    0.602  0.053    0.524  1.9040e-10  2.166e-11       1.205   0.98    -0.151
SPARC          409     0.451  0.028    0.525  0.044    0.528  1.3032e-10  1.609e-11       1.050   1.44    -0.065
HI              25     0.667  0.215      nan  0.190    0.514  1.4471e-10  5.024e-11         nan   1.29    -0.050

  POOLED (386 deep rings): ring-pooled beta = 0.452 +- 0.025 -> n = 0.903 +- 0.049
    per-sample equal-weight: beta = 0.522 +- 0.059 (between-sample se) -> n = 1.043 +- 0.119
    per-galaxy reading (SPARC+MIGHTEE per-gal medians, HI pooled): beta = 0.598 +- 0.034 -> n = 1.196 +- 0.067
    pooled deep a0_fit = 1.3836e-10 -> n_amp(pooled) = 1.353

--- PART 3: THE STATISTICS (sigma separations vs the two footings) ---
  SLOPE CHANNEL (n = 2*beta, the task-declared relation):
  MIGHTEE pooled                               n =  0.893 +- 0.091 | vs 2.000: -12.1 sigma | vs 1.660: -8.4 sigma
  MIGHTEE per-galaxy                           n =  1.205 +- 0.105 | vs 2.000: -7.6 sigma | vs 1.660: -4.3 sigma
  SPARC pooled                                 n =  0.902 +- 0.056 | vs 2.000: -19.6 sigma | vs 1.660: -13.5 sigma
  SPARC per-galaxy                             n =  1.050 +- 0.088 | vs 2.000: -10.8 sigma | vs 1.660: -6.9 sigma
  HI (pooled, single points)                   n =  1.335 +- 0.430 | vs 2.000: -1.5 sigma | vs 1.660: -0.8 sigma
  POOLED ring-level                            n =  0.903 +- 0.049 | vs 2.000: -22.3 sigma | vs 1.660: -15.4 sigma
  POOLED per-galaxy reading                    n =  1.196 +- 0.067 | vs 2.000: -12.0 sigma | vs 1.660: -6.9 sigma
  AMPLITUDE CHANNEL (n = s_Lambda/a0_eff, the seesaw itself):
  MIGHTEE                                      n =  0.983 +- 0.112 | vs 2.000: -9.1 sigma | vs 1.660: -6.0 sigma
  SPARC deep rings                             n =  1.437 +- 0.177 | vs 2.000: -3.2 sigma | vs 1.660: -1.3 sigma
  HI deep dwarfs                               n =  1.294 +- 0.449 | vs 2.000: -1.6 sigma | vs 1.660: -0.8 sigma
  POOLED (fit over all deep rings)      n =  1.353 (a0_fit = 1.384e-10) -- BUT the
         three deep samples are mutually inconsistent on the amplitude (n = 0.98 / 1.44 / 1.29); the honest pooled
         amplitude reading is n = 1.24 +- 0.19 (sample-to-sample std: no single deep-end n exists across lanes)

  THE SUPERLUMINALITY KILL: H046 G1: in the minimal Pade family n <= 2;
  a measured n even 1% above 2 (n > 2.01) kills the completion.
    SLOPE pooled (per-galaxy reading): n =  1.196 +- 0.067 -> (2.01 - n)/sigma = +12.1 (no kill)
    SLOPE ring-pooled         : n =  0.903 +- 0.049 -> (2.01 - n)/sigma = +22.5 (no kill)
    AMP MIGHTEE               : n =  0.983 +- 0.112 -> (2.01 - n)/sigma = +9.2 (no kill)
    AMP SPARC deep            : n =  1.437 +- 0.177 -> (2.01 - n)/sigma = +3.2 (no kill)

--- PART 4: THE WEDGE (the honest converse) ---
  MIGHTEE deep-end offset vs the committed amplitude (G099 register):
    at a0_DE     : deep median -0.151 dex  (obs/pred = 1.42x, G099: -0.151, 9.9 sigma)
    at a0_ALT    : deep median -0.111 dex  (obs/pred = 1.29x -- partially closed, G099: -0.111)
    at a0 = 1.843e-10 (G133 fit): deep median +0.008 dex -- CLOSED at the MIGHTEE scale
  the ALT footing closes the offset only partially: 0.151 -> 0.111 dex; it closes
  fully at a0 ~ 1.84e-10, where the seesaw gives n = 1.016 -- not 1.660.
  THE WEDGE: the deep end wants the LARGER a0 (a0_eff ~ 1.2-1.9e-10, i.e. n_amp ~ 0.99-1.56) and the programme's mode count wants n = 2.000
    at a0 = 1.1279e-10: n = 1.660 (the ALT footing's own value -- consistent with SPARC-deep)
    at a0 = 1.843e-10 : n = 1.016 (MIGHTEE -- 2.000 excluded at 7 sigma, 1.660 at 5 sigma)
    log a0 gap DE->MIGHTEE: +0.294 dex = +5.1 sigma (G133, log) -- the deep end's scale is RAR-class, not DE-class.
  JOINT statement: (a0_deep_end = 1.2-1.9e-10) AND (n = 2.000) cannot both hold if
  n(a0) = s/a0 runs: the pair is excluded at the MIGHTEE step by 5.1 sigma (log) /
  7.3 sigma (linear n);
  the ONE deep-end reading consistent with n = 2.000 would need a0 = 9.3619e-11 --
  which the deep end rejects (MIGHTEE +1.97x at 5.1 sigma-log; SPARC deep rings -1.5x).

--- PART 5: VERDICTS ---
  V1 THE MEASURED DEEP EXPONENTS (per sample + pooled, both channels):
    SLOPE channel (n = 2*beta):  MIGHTEE 0.89 +- 0.09 (pooled) / 1.20 +- 0.11 (per-gal) | 
      SPARC 0.90 +- 0.06 (pooled) / 1.05 +- 0.09 (per-gal) | HI 1.33 +- 0.43 | 
      pooled: 1.20 +- 0.07 (per-galaxy reading) | 0.90 +- 0.05 (ring-level)
    AMPLITUDE channel (n = s/a0_eff): MIGHTEE 0.98, SPARC-deep 1.44, HI 1.29, pooled-fit 1.35 (samples mutually inconsistent: 0.98/1.44/1.29)
  V2 THE SEPARATION (vs 2.000 and 1.660, sigma):
    slope channel:  vs 2.000: 12.0 sigma (per-gal pooled), 22.3 sigma (ring pooled) | vs 1.660: 6.9 sigma (per-gal pooled), 15.4 sigma (ring pooled)
    amplitude channel: MIGHTEE vs 2.000: 9.1 sigma, vs 1.660: 6.0 sigma | SPARC-deep vs 2.000: 3.2 sigma, vs 1.660: 1.3 sigma
  [PASS] C1 [relation] the law's own deep-window slope is the quadratic ~0.50-0.58 (beta_law = n/2 with n ~ 1.0-1.2), so n = 2*beta of the deep asymptote is the form, not the footing   SPARC beta_law 0.528, MIGHTEE 0.524
  [PASS] C2 [slope-channel discriminator] the pooled deep slope excludes BOTH seesaw footings' predicted beta = n/2 (1.000 and 0.830) at > 3 sigma   n = 1.20 +- 0.07; vs 2.000: 12.0s, vs 1.660: 6.9s
  [PASS] C3 [amplitude discriminator] the largest deep sample's amplitude n = s/a0_eff excludes BOTH footings at > 3 sigma (MIGHTEE a0 = 1.90e-10 on the deep window)   n = 0.983 +- 0.112; vs 2.000: 9s, vs 1.660: 6s
  [PASS] C4 [no superluminality kill] the measured n +- sigma sits > 3 sigma BELOW the n = 2.01 kill line (1% above the n = 2 bound)   (2.01 - 1.20)/0.07 = +12.1 sigma
  [PASS] C5 [the wedge] 'deep end wants the LARGER a0 AND n = 2.000' is quantified: at the deep end's own scale (1.843e-10, G133) the seesaw gives n ~ 1.0, excluding the n = 2.000 joint claim at > 5 sigma   n(1.843e-10) = 1.016; (2.000 - 1.016) = 7 sigma

  V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT -- does today's deep data adjudicate the footings?  YES, against the DE-anchored n = 2.000, and against n = 1.660 in the slope channel; the wedge sharpens into a real tension at ~5 sigma.  THE NUMBERS.  (1) The deep RAR slope over g_N < 0.2 a0 measures beta = 0.598 +- 0.034 per-galaxy (ring-pooled 0.452 +- 0.025, flattened by galaxy-mixing): the asymptotic form is the quadratic 1/2, whose window-exponent is n = 2*beta = 1.20 +- 0.07; the seesaw footings predict beta = n/2 = 1.000 (n = 2.000) and 0.830 (n = 1.660) -- excluded at 12.0 sigma and 6.9 sigma (per-galaxy pooled) respectively.  (2) The deep-end AMPLITUDE (the seesaw itself, n = s/a0_eff): MIGHTEE n = 0.98 +- 0.11 (a0 = 1.90e-10); SPARC deep rings n = 1.44 +- 0.18 (a0 = 1.30e-10 -- the sub-DE end of the deep rings); HI dwarfs n = 1.29 +- 0.45 (a0 = 1.45e-10).  The deep-end samples are mutually inconsistent on the amplitude (MIGHTEE +1.9x vs DE, SPARC-deep -1.5x) but NONE sits at n = 2.000: the DE footing is excluded by every deep-end reading at >= 3 sigma, and MIGHTEE -- the largest deep sample -- excludes even n = 1.660 at 6 sigma.  (3) THE WEDGE: the deep end wants the LARGER a0 (1.2-1.9e-10, RAR-class) AND the full-curve mode count wants n = 2.000 at a0 = 9.3619e-11; with n(a0) = s/a0 running, the pair is jointly inconsistent: at the deep end's own preferred scale a0 = 1.843e-10 the seesaw gives n = 1.016, i.e. the n = 2.000 claim fails by the deep-end offset (MIGHTEE +0.15 dex deep, 5.1 sigma-log, G133; the offset closes only at the MIGHTEE scale where n ~ 1.0).  The ALT footing n = 1.660 is the deep end's SPARC-consistent value and its amplitude is the closest deep-end reading to the data, but the deep SLOPE still excludes its n/2 = 0.830 at ~6.9 sigma (the slope is the quadratic 1/2).  KILL CHECK: the measured n sits 12.1 sigma BELOW the n = 2.01 superluminal kill line -- no kill, the deep end is nowhere near n > 2 by 1pct; the danger is instead the OPPOSITE one: every deep-end channel reads n <= 1.7, i.e. the observed n does NOT saturate the subluminality bound at the deep end (the saturation claim rests on the full-curve L232 rms separation of 0.016 dex, not on the deep end).
  [PASS] V3 [statement]   V3 THE HONEST STATEMENT -- does today's deep data adjudicate the footings?  YES, against the DE-anchored n = 2.000, and against n = 1.660 in the slope channel; the wedge sharpens into a real tension at ~5 sigma.  THE NUMBERS.  (1) The deep RAR slope over g_N < 0.2 a0 measures beta = 0.598 +- 0.034 per-galaxy (ring-pooled 0.452 +- 0.025, flattened by galaxy-mixing): the asymptotic form is the quadratic 1/2, whose window-exponent is n = 2*beta = 1.20 +- 0.07; the seesaw footings predict beta = n/2 = 1.000 (n = 2.000) and 0.830 (n = 1.660) -- excluded at 12.0 sigma and 6.9 sigma (per-galaxy pooled) respectively.  (2) The deep-end AMPLITUDE (the seesaw itself, n = s/a0_eff): MIGHTEE n = 0.98 +- 0.11 (a0 = 1.90e-10); SPARC deep rings n = 1.44 +- 0.18 (a0 = 1.30e-10 -- the sub-DE end of the deep rings); HI dwarfs n = 1.29 +- 0.45 (a0 = 1.45e-10).  The deep-end samples are mutually inconsistent on the amplitude (MIGHTEE +1.9x vs DE, SPARC-deep -1.5x) but NONE sits at n = 2.000: the DE footing is excluded by every deep-end reading at >= 3 sigma, and MIGHTEE -- the largest deep sample -- excludes even n = 1.660 at 6 sigma.  (3) THE WEDGE: the deep end wants the LARGER a0 (1.2-1.9e-10, RAR-class) AND the full-curve mode count wants n = 2.000 at a0 = 9.3619e-11; with n(a0) = s/a0 running, the pair is jointly inconsistent: at the deep end's own preferred scale a0 = 1.843e-10 the seesaw gives n = 1.016, i.e. the n = 2.000 claim fails by the deep-end offset (MIGHTEE +0.15 dex deep, 5.1 sigma-log, G133; the offset closes only at the MIGHTEE scale where n ~ 1.0).  The ALT footing n = 1.660 is the deep end's SPARC-consistent value and its amplitude is the closest deep-end reading to the data, but the deep SLOPE still excludes its n/2 = 0.830 at ~6.9 sigma (the slope is the quadratic 1/2).  KILL CHECK: the measured n sits 12.1 sigma BELOW the n = 2.01 superluminal kill line -- no kill, the deep end is nowhere near n > 2 by 1pct; the danger is instead the OPPOSITE one: every deep-end channel reads n <= 1.7, i.e. the observed n does NOT saturate the subluminality bound at the deep end (the saturation claim rests on the full-curve L232 rms separation of 0.016 dex, not on the deep end).

